Subject: [PATCH] doc: org.bluez.Adapter: document AddRemoteLegacyOOB

---
 doc/org.bluez.Adapter.rst | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/org.bluez.Adapter.rst b/doc/org.bluez.Adapter.rst
index c84490d..e7d6656 100644
--- a/doc/org.bluez.Adapter.rst
+++ b/doc/org.bluez.Adapter.rst
@@ -246,6 +246,54 @@ Possible errors:
 :org.bluez.Error.NotReady:
 :org.bluez.Error.Failed:
 
+void AddRemoteLegacyOOB(string address, string address_type, array{byte} tk)
+``````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````````
+
+Supplies the 128-bit LE legacy Security Manager Temporary Key for a peer that
+requires out-of-band pairing on the *legacy* (non-Secure-Connections) LE
+pairing path — a Just Works or passkey Pairing Request from this adapter would
+otherwise be rejected outright by such a peer. Requires a patched kernel: see
+Documentation/networking/bluetooth-le-legacy-oob.rst upstream (mainline BlueZ
+targets a kernel with no such interface today).
+
+The kernel arms the key for exactly one pairing attempt with this identity: it
+is consumed on a successful pairing and kept (not re-usable, but not wiped
+either) across a failed one, so a retry does not need this method called
+again, but a *second successful* pairing with the same peer does. Call
+**Device1.Pair()** (or an equivalent directed-connect + pair) immediately
+after; do not cache and reuse a `tk` across bonds.
+
+:string address:
+
+	The Bluetooth address of the remote device, in the identity address the
+	adapter will connect to — not a resolvable private address.
+
+:string address_type:
+
+	Possible values:
+
+	:"public":
+
+		Public address.
+
+	:"random":
+
+		Static random address.
+
+:array{byte} tk:
+
+	The 16-byte Temporary Key, in the byte order the peer's out-of-band
+	channel delivered it (Security Manager wire order — do not reverse it).
+
+Possible errors:
+
+:org.bluez.Error.InvalidArguments: Bad address, address type, or a `tk` that
+	is not exactly 16 bytes.
+:org.bluez.Error.NotReady: Adapter is not powered.
+:org.bluez.Error.Failed: The kernel rejected the command (see the kernel log
+	for the exact reason — commonly means the kernel does not support this
+	extended `Add Remote OOB Data` payload).
+
